    "body": "This PR clarifies a few details of BIP138's binary encoding.\r\n\r\nIt adds two test vectors in a new `payload.json`, but shouldn't be a breaking change.\r\n\r\nThree middle commits:\r\n\r\n- _specify empty associated data_: make the AAD input explicit in the encryption and decryption formulas.\r\n- _clarify that 0x00 ends payload parsing_: add a test vector with a content item followed by a terminator and ignored bytes.\r\n- _clarify rejection of empty payloads_: add a test vector containing only the terminator, with zero content items.\r\n\r\nThe first commit introduces a changelog. I'm reusing that commit across a few parallel pull requests.\r\n\r\nThe last commit updates the changelog; I'll update that depending on merge order.",
